Hi Gonçalo, the issue is that oSCR expects the occasion number to be sequential (1:K) within a session.  This requires some tweaking to your data flow:

Line 153
day_number <- as.integer(as.Date(date, format = "%Y-%m-%d") - date_intervals[[i]][1]) + 1

Line 170
# Convert the `occ` column from dates to day numbers relative to the base date
#edf <- edf %>%
#  mutate(occ = as.integer(as.Date(occ, format = "%Y-%m-%d") - base_date) + 1)
for (i in 1:nrow(edf)){
  edf$occ2[i] <- as.integer(as.Date(edf$occ[i], format = "%Y-%m-%d") - date_intervals[[edf$sessionID[[i]]]][1]) + 1
}

These modifications use session-specific date origins (from the date intervals) to identify occasion number.  This assumes no gaps.  Either way it allows your code to work with data2oscr.

